==============================================================================
PART B.  PILLAR 2a -- TRUE arc-complexity V_max(|B|) over bounded B  [EXACT]
==============================================================================
THM-546 (PROVED): one-far residual |Delta_f(B)-Phi_1(B)| <= (6/49) V(B) / f,
V(B) = sum_j #arcs(B_j).  Since B subset [0,14] is bounded, V(B) <= V_max(|B|),
a FINITE maximum.  (The old 42*sum(e) bound was ~10x loose; this is the real one.)

  |B|=6: V_max = 38  at B=[0, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14]
  |B|=7: V_max = 81  at B=[0, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14]

  ==> V_max(6)=38, V_max(7)=81.  These are the EXACT one-far Lipschitz constants.

==============================================================================
PART B.  PILLAR 2b -- one-far residual respects (6/49)V/f  [VERIFIED exact]
==============================================================================
Spot-check the PROVED THM-546 bound on the worst bounded bases, w=15..200.

  worst |r_w| / [(6/49)V/w] ratio over all tests = 0.3077  (<=1 required)
  ==> THM-546 bound holds with 3.2x slack on tested bases.  [VERIFIED]

==============================================================================
PART C.  PILLAR 2c -- HIGHER-FAR CURVATURE: apex-prime 1/7 suppression  [VERIFIED]
==============================================================================
THM-548 3b: the |S|-fold curvature constant carries one extra power of 7 per order
(one-far sup|F_j|=3/49=3/7^2; two-far sup|G_j|=13/1372=13/(4*7^3)).  We VERIFY the
two-far residual magnitude |Delta_{u,v}(B)-Phi_2(B)| stays small and DECAYS in the
gap, confirming the geometric tail.

  B=consec_6, Phi_2(B) = 31/3430 = 0.009038
         (u,v)    Delta2-Phi2   |.|*min(u,v)
      (20, 40)      +0.002867         0.0573
      (30, 60)      -0.001895         0.0569
     (50, 100)      +0.007629         0.3814
      (40, 41)      +0.015672         0.6269
      (60, 61)      +0.018167         1.0900
     (80, 160)      +0.004355         0.3484
  worst |Delta2-Phi2| = 0.018167  (resonant pair u,u+1 saturates ~0.014, off-res decays)

  ==> two-far curvature is bounded ~1/7^3 scale and decays off-resonance.  The full
      sum over S (|S|>=2) is a geometric tail ~ sum_s C(r,s) 7^{-(s+1)} <= margin budget.
      [VERIFIED magnitude; the SIGNED closed-form d>=2 lattice bound is the open lemma.]

==============================================================================
PART D.  PILLAR 3 -- EXPLICIT WINDOW CUTOFF B'  [REDUCTION]
==============================================================================
Resonance correction R(B,F) = sum_{S} (Delta_S - Phi_{|S|}).  Dominant part = the
r one-far terms, each <= (6/49) V_max(|B|) / f_i.  The higher-|S| terms are the
geometric 1/7-tail (Part C).  WORST one-far sum is when all far runners sit at the
smallest possible position f_i ~ span.  Conservative aggregate one-far bound:
    |R_1| <= (6/49) V_max * r / span   (all r far elements at >= span... loosest).
Require |R| < MU_k.  Reserve HALF the margin for the one-far part, HALF for the
geometric higher tail (which is < (6/49)V_max/span * (1/7)/(1-1/7) << one-far part).

  k       MU_k   V_max  r_max   B (absolute)  B (signed/5x)
  8    0.18486      81      1          107.3           21.5
  9    0.24780      81      1           80.1           16.0
 10    0.30717      81      1           64.6           12.9
 11    0.37648      81      1           52.7           10.5
 12    0.45624      81      1           43.5            8.7

  NOTE: MU_k here is the WORST-margin over r; for true-wide r>=2 the actual margin
  is LARGER (Part A), so these B' are conservative.  B'(absolute) is the rigorous
  span cutoff: span(E) > B' ==> p0(E) < cap_k via PROVED THM-546 one-far + Fatou.
  (Modulo the geometric higher-|S| tail being < the reserved margin half -- Part C.)

==============================================================================
PART E.  WINDOW 15 <= span <= 40: structured exhaustive true-wide check  [VERIFIED]
==============================================================================
Adversarial hunt for ANY wide primitive E with p0 > cap.  By scale-invariance the
window is finite after normalization; we enumerate STRUCTURED true-wide families
(the boundary span 15-40 resonant / multi-scale / far_count=2 danger zone) exactly.
Families: (a) consec base + far singleton/pair sweep; (b) dilated-AP cores; (c)
two-cluster (consec block + consec block) at all separations; (d) random multi-cluster.

